  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.5907 accuracy. Image alone (resnet50) is very weak (0.2079), raising the question of whether adding it in fusion provides any complementary signal. Config_018 extends the proven best RNA configuration by adding resnet50 image features with concat fusion while keeping the same multiprofile + avgpool setup, isolating the effect of multimodal fusion. This is the highest-value experiment because: (1) it directly tests whether the weak image modality adds information beyond strong RNA, (2) if it helps, the remaining 4 experiments can optimize fusion strategy (weighted), image encoder (ViT-L), or RNA encoder; if it doesn't, we can redirect budget to RNA-only improvements like scvi_n200 with multiprofile. Testing the simplest fusion (concat) with the best-known RNA setup first avoids confounding multiple changes."
}

